{
  "file": "crates/habeas-sdk/tests/agent.rs",
  "item": "fn[agent_edge_tools_record_selections_without_validating_targets]/impl[Render/AgentInputRenderer<GraphWithChangingEdges>]/fn[render]",
  "citations": [
    {
      "role": "cite",
      "name": "habeas:coverage",
      "commentary": "The agent asks only for outgoing edges and submits without reading\n contents. Its renderer is required by the agent interface, but any\n rendering would imply an unwanted content input. Other agent tests\n exercise rendering with explicitly requested contents."
    }
  ],
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The `habeas:coverage` citation is on an explicit function with a body, `fn[render]` in the `Render` impl inside `agent_edge_tools_record_selections_without_validating_targets`. Its commentary is fenced citation commentary, which the built-in accepts as a tracked explanation.\n\nThe explanation is substantive and agrees with the source:\n- `render` is a deliberate `panic!` guard. The test script in the same function only calls `outgoing_edges` and then `submit_result`, so no content is ever requested or rendered. The test also asserts that the recorded dependency is only `Dependency::OutgoingEdges`.\n- `Validator::with_agent` in `crates/habeas-sdk/src/graph/runtime.rs` takes an `Arc<dyn AgentInputRenderer<D>>`. A renderer is therefore required, as the commentary says.\n- Other tests do exercise rendering with real contents. `Renderer` and `DistinctPages` in `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/agent.rs` return the node contents from `render`. `RejectContents` returns an error from `render`.\n\nThe justification is a specific reason the function is not executed, not just difficulty. The citation is not redundant with any `{impl}` or `{test}` reference on the item.",
